WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.127 --> 00:00:02.340
(tense music)
(snow rumbling)

00:00:02.340 --> 00:00:06.410
- [Man] Serious storm; we are
at war with Mother Nature.

00:00:06.410 --> 00:00:08.800
These avalanches can be
deadly, and the best way

00:00:08.800 --> 00:00:10.923
to mitigate 'em is with explosives.

00:00:12.020 --> 00:00:14.750
Here at Mammoth Mountain,
it's a blast from the past.

00:00:14.750 --> 00:00:17.063
We literally use World War II cannons.

00:00:17.063 --> 00:00:18.317
Charge!

00:00:18.317 --> 00:00:21.067
(dramatic music)

00:00:22.797 --> 00:00:24.461
(explosion booming)
- Detonation!

00:00:24.461 --> 00:00:26.044
- [Man] Detonation.

00:00:26.956 --> 00:00:29.956
(suspenseful music)

00:00:31.460 --> 00:00:32.907
- My name's Matt Seibert.

00:00:32.907 --> 00:00:35.003
I'm a Mammoth Mountain ski patroller.

00:00:36.820 --> 00:00:39.230
On any given day, we can see

00:00:39.230 --> 00:00:42.647
anywhere between 5,000 and 18,000 guests.

00:00:42.647 --> 00:00:45.930
(light music)

00:00:45.930 --> 00:00:48.120
We try to keep a constant
watch on the mountain

00:00:48.120 --> 00:00:49.619
and changing conditions

00:00:49.619 --> 00:00:52.746
to create the safest environment possible.

00:00:52.746 --> 00:00:55.246
(light music)

00:00:57.620 --> 00:01:00.990
Steep slopes, large
snowfall, intense winds.

00:01:00.990 --> 00:01:03.982
They're all recipes for an avalanche.

00:01:03.982 --> 00:01:08.982
(snow rumbling)
(light music)

00:01:13.810 --> 00:01:15.620
- I've worked in our artillery program

00:01:15.620 --> 00:01:18.283
here on Mammoth Mountain
for the past seven years.

00:01:19.600 --> 00:01:23.090
The howitzer was originally
a World War II weapon of war.

00:01:23.090 --> 00:01:25.190
Now discontinued in the war theater,

00:01:25.190 --> 00:01:28.083
it is now a valuable tool
for avalanche mitigation.

00:01:30.210 --> 00:01:33.810
Our whole team feels secure
when the gun goes out and fires.

00:01:33.810 --> 00:01:35.970
It's able to reach targets
that we would not normally

00:01:35.970 --> 00:01:38.569
be able to reach with just
throwing hand charges.

00:01:38.569 --> 00:01:39.452
- [Man] Fire!

00:01:39.452 --> 00:01:44.430
(explosion booming)
- Detonation! Clear to reach.

00:01:44.430 --> 00:01:48.590
Our intent is to create many
small controlled avalanches.

00:01:48.590 --> 00:01:51.000
As opposed to letting the snow rest

00:01:51.000 --> 00:01:54.523
and winding up with one
large, devastating avalanche.

00:01:56.000 --> 00:01:59.470
We fire our gun 90% of
the time blind in a storm

00:01:59.470 --> 00:02:01.750
without being able to see our target.

00:02:01.750 --> 00:02:05.100
We are capable of dialing
in on one tiny little rock

00:02:05.100 --> 00:02:06.843
and nailing it on the nose.

00:02:06.843 --> 00:02:08.264
- Fire!

00:02:08.264 --> 00:02:12.536
(explosion booming)
- Detonation! - Detonation!

00:02:12.536 --> 00:02:14.570
(light music)

00:02:14.570 --> 00:02:16.529
The risks are real.

00:02:16.529 --> 00:02:18.850
- [Man] Uh, upper mountain wind slack

00:02:18.850 --> 00:02:20.851
is considerable danger.

00:02:20.851 --> 00:02:22.970
- [Matt] Each day we arrive at work

00:02:22.970 --> 00:02:25.771
we put our name on the
board for accountability.

00:02:25.771 --> 00:02:28.010
(light music)

00:02:28.010 --> 00:02:30.470
- We go out together; we work together.

00:02:30.470 --> 00:02:33.010
At the end of the day,
we come in together.

00:02:33.010 --> 00:02:37.510
Take our name off the board,
and we don't stop work

00:02:37.510 --> 00:02:40.253
until the last one of
us is in for the day.

00:02:42.367 --> 00:02:43.200
(light music)

00:02:43.200 --> 00:02:45.880
I do take joy knowing that there

00:02:45.880 --> 00:02:48.870
are families out here
recreating, having fun,

00:02:48.870 --> 00:02:52.630
bringing up the next generation
of skiers and snowboarders.

00:02:52.630 --> 00:02:54.456
Enjoying the mountain.

00:02:54.456 --> 00:02:55.400
(light music)

00:02:55.400 --> 00:02:57.870
It's a job I love, and

00:02:57.870 --> 00:02:59.180
it's my goal to create

00:02:59.180 --> 00:03:01.547
the safest environment for our guests.

00:03:01.547 --> 00:03:04.547
(light music fades)

00:03:09.001 --> 00:03:11.418
(bell dings)

